meta {
  name: explain why recent requests did not match any expectation
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/mockserver/explainUnmatched
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "limit": 5
  }
}

docs {
  Returns a diagnostic report for recently recorded unmatched requests, including the closest-matching expectations and the per-field differences that prevented a match. An optional 'limit' in the body bounds how many unmatched requests are analysed (default 10). With 'suggestFixes' set to true, each of the five closest non-matching expectations also carries a 'suggestedFix': an RFC 6902 JSON patch of that expectation (as PUT /mockserver/retrieve?type=active_expectations returns it) that would make it match the request, the fields it patches and cannot patch, and whether the patched expectation matches. Nothing is applied: to apply a fix, patch the retrieved expectation and send it to PUT /mockserver/expectation, which updates the expectation with the same id. Values the event log redacts are never copied into a patch.
  
  optional limit on the number of unmatched requests to analyse
  
  Full API reference: https://www.mock-server.com/mock_server/mockserver_clients.html
}
